 },
 "capsule": "The Kingdom of Georgia was the unified Bagrationi monarchy created by Bagrat III's consolidation of Abkhazia, Kartli, Kakheti and Tao by 1010, reaching its political and cultural apex under David IV 'the Builder' (1089-1125), who expelled the Seljuks and retook Tbilisi in 1122, and under Queen Tamar (1184-1213), whose reign is remembered as Georgia's Golden Age. After the Mongol invasions of the 1220s-1240s the kingdom survived as a fragmented tributary state, weathered further Timurid invasions, and by the 1490s splintered into the separate kingdoms of Kartli, Kakheti and Imereti. The 'Kingdom of Georgia' name nonetheless persisted for the eastern Kartli-Kakheti crown until its final annexation by the Russian Empire in 1801-1803.",
